From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: burntcarrot <aadhav.n1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 02 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 30/31] kernel: seed-controlled task selection in DeterministicScheduler

Background:
Patch 0003 used a TID min-heap for task selection — always picks the
lowest TID. This is deterministic but explores only ONE interleaving of
container execution. Real distributed systems bugs (Raft split-brain,
stale reads, lost-update races) manifest only under specific interleavings.

Antithesis explores multiple interleavings via random VM scheduling. We
go further: seed-controlled random selection at the SYSCALL level. Every
syscall boundary is a potential context-switch point. The RNG (seeded from
--openthesis-dst-seed) determines which task runs at each such point.

This means:
  - Same seed → same scheduling sequence → exact bug reproduction
  - Different seeds → different orderings → finds different race conditions
  - Combined with AFL-style coverage guidance: focus seeds that produce
    new edge coverage → systematic exploration of all interleavings

Design:
Replace taskHeap (container/heap min-heap) with a flat []*Task slice.
Replace heap.Pop(min-TID) with rng.Int63n(len(runnable)) random pick.

When rng is nil (no RNG set yet, or DST mode not fully initialized),
fall back to index-0 selection (deterministic, consistent with old
lowest-TID behavior since tasks are appended in creation order).

Changes:
1. dst_scheduler.go — DeterministicScheduler struct:
   - Replace runnable taskHeap with runnable []*Task
   - Add rng *DeterministicRNG field

2. dst_scheduler.go — NewDeterministicScheduler():
   - No changes to constructor (rng set via SetRNG later)

3. dst_scheduler.go — Schedule() loop:
   - Replace heap.Pop with seeded random pick from runnable slice
   - Replace heap.Push with append for re-queueing

4. dst_scheduler.go — MakeRunnable():
   - Replace heap.Push with append

5. dst_scheduler.go — SetRNG() (new method):
   - Called from runsc/boot/loader.go after InitDST() to wire the DST RNG

6. runsc/boot/loader.go — wire SetRNG after sched initialization:
   - sched.SetRNG(rng) so the same RNG used for all DST decisions also
     controls task scheduling order
